  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I could not run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Bars:** 64 boxes sit on a ring of radius 5 and stand on a floor plane. They are one instanced box node, so they draw in a single call.\n- **Animation:** each frame, `setInstanceMatrices` rewrites all 64 transforms with heights from four summed sine waves. The phases differ per bar and over time.\n- **Colour:** each bar gets its own hue from an even gradient around the ring. The material is white so the colour isn't applied twice.\n- **Lighting:** there is a hemisphere light, a neutral environment, a PCF soft-shadow key light and a blue fill light. Bars cast and receive shadows, and the floor receives them.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera with `autoRotate: 0.15` rad/s circles the ring. Dragging the canvas will also move it.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after the first `onFrame` update.\n- **Build:** I did not use top-level `await`, because Vite's default build target may reject it.\n\nI didn't check how soft the shadows look, because I had no rendered frame. If they look too hard, raise the `softness` value on the key light.\n\n",
